  "findings": [
    "A cluster makes a big model possible, not fast. With the HP Z820 at 64 GB, the 83 GiB Qwen3.8-Flash-Next fitted neither PC, and two PCs together ran it at 1.69 to 2.45 tokens a second.",
    "Once one PC can hold the model, it is faster alone. With 256 GB the HP Z820 ran the same model alone at 7.20, against 2.85 to 4.14 in the cluster.",
    "For a model that fits one PC, use that PC, with one exception seen: lending a fast card made reading a long prompt about four times faster, while writing stayed slower.",
    "Three PCs were not better than two: from less than half to about one and a half times the speed of two, and long loads failed.",
    "A model bigger than the RAM, read from an SSD instead: not measured, so no figure."
  ]
}
